# 18. COMPETITION JUDGING REQUIREMENTS

The application must target the strongest standard on all five criteria.

TRACEABILITY — 25%
Every prediction must be reconstructible from raw data to output.

UNSEEN TESTING — 25%
Every strategy must face locked, previously unseen datasets, adversarial scenarios, appropriate baselines and realistic costs.

RISK AND OVERSIGHT — 15%
Risk limits must be enforced in code, with human approval and demonstrable rejection of unsafe paper trades.

RELEVANCE AND IMPACT — 20%
The platform must solve the genuine research problem of converting fragmented real-world information into credible, actionable financial hypotheses.

AMBITION AND TECHNICAL QUALITY — 15%
Show genuine autonomous hypothesis generation, mathematical model design, alternative-data forecasting, independent criticism and production-quality engineering.

Create a dedicated judge-facing evaluation page.

Allow judges to inspect:
- Raw data.
- Research hypotheses.
- Generated models.
- Backtests.
- Failures.
- Risk controls.
- Research reports.
- Reproducibility records.

Provide an end-to-end demonstration using unseen or previously locked data.

